---
{% extends "shell.njk" %}{% block body %}
{% set shipped = releases.releases %}
{% set retiring = releases.retirements %}
{# Mirrors the JS formatters below so the server-rendered table reads the same
   with JS off. `r.in` is quoted for clarity: `in` is an operator in the template
   language, and a dash beats printing a price the lab never published. #}
{% macro usd(v) %}{% if v === null or v === undefined or v === "" %}&mdash;{% else %}${{ v }}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{% macro ctx(n) %}{% if not n %}&mdash;{% elif n >= 1000000 %}{{ (n / 1000000) | round(2) }}M{% else %}{{ (n / 1000) | round }}K{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
<div class="eye">FREE TOOL · WHAT SHIPPED, WHAT'S LEAVING</div>
<h1 class="page-title">AI Model Release <em>Tracker.</em></h1>
<p class="lede">Every new model the major labs have put into production in the last 45 days, with the price you would actually pay, and every model they have announced they are switching off. Two lists, because the second one is the one that reaches your invoice unannounced.</p>

<div class="tracker-bar">
  <div class="filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter by lab">
    <button type="button" class="chip is-on" data-lab="all">All labs</button>
    {% for lab in releases.labs %}
    <button type="button" class="chip" data-lab="{{ lab }}">{{ lab }}</button>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <p class="freshness">Snapshot <strong>{{ releases.updated }}</strong><span id="liveCheck"></span></p>
</div>

<h2>New in the last 45 days <span class="count">{{ shipped | length }} models</span></h2>
<p class="note">A model appears here the day it first became purchasable through a public router. It usually trails the lab's own announcement by a few days. Prices are USD per 1M tokens, straight from the router's rate card.</p>
<div class="table-wrap">
  <table class="tracker-table" id="shippedTable">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">First available</th>
        <th scope="col">Model</th>
        <th scope="col">Lab</th>
        <th scope="col" class="num">Input / 1M</th>
        <th scope="col" class="num">Output / 1M</th>
        <th scope="col" class="num">Context</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for r in shipped %}
      <tr data-lab="{{ r.provider }}" data-id="{{ r.id }}">
        <td><time datetime="{{ r.date }}">{{ r.date }}</time></td>
        <td><strong>{{ r.id }}</strong></td>
        <td>{{ r.provider }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ usd(r["in"]) }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ usd(r["out"]) }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ ctx(r.ctx) }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p class="empty" id="shippedEmpty" hidden>No models from that lab in this window.</p>

<h2>Announced retirements <span class="count">{{ retiring | length }} models</span></h2>
<p class="note">Dates a lab or router has published for switching a model off. A model on this list is not deprecated-yet: on the date shown, calls to it start failing. Price is included so the replacement can be costed in the same column.</p>
<div class="table-wrap">
  <table class="tracker-table" id="retiringTable">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Switch-off date</th>
        <th scope="col">In</th>
        <th scope="col">Model</th>
        <th scope="col">Lab</th>
        <th scope="col" class="num">Input / 1M</th>
        <th scope="col" class="num">Output / 1M</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for r in retiring %}
      <tr data-lab="{{ r.provider }}" data-id="{{ r.id }}" data-expires="{{ r.expires }}" class="{% if r.daysLeft <= 30 %}is-urgent{% endif %}">
        <td><time datetime="{{ r.expires }}">{{ r.expires }}</time></td>
        <td class="left"><span class="days" data-days>{{ r.daysLeft }}d</span></td>
        <td><strong>{{ r.id }}</strong></td>
        <td>{{ r.provider }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ usd(r["in"]) }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ usd(r["out"]) }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p class="empty" id="retiringEmpty" hidden>Nothing announced for that lab.</p>

<div class="methodology">
<h2>Why the second table is the one that costs you</h2>
<p>A new model is a decision. A retirement is an event, and it arrives whether or not anyone on your team was watching. Three things break quietly on a switch-off date:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Routing rules.</strong> A load balancer or fallback chain that still references the retired id returns errors for that slice of traffic. If the fallback was never load-tested, the retry path becomes the primary path and your latency bill follows.</li>
<li><strong>Evaluation baselines.</strong> Any score, prompt or guardrail tuned against the old model's behaviour is now measuring a system that no longer exists. Regression alerts that fire afterwards are noise, and the ones that don't fire are worse.</li>
<li><strong>Prompts tuned to a context window.</strong> A replacement with a smaller ceiling truncates mid-document. The failure is a plausible answer built on half the input, which is far more expensive to catch than an error.</li>
</ul>
<p>The cheapest time to price a replacement is before the switch-off date, while the old model still runs and you can measure both side by side on real traffic. That is the whole argument for keeping this list rather than reading about it after the fact.</p>

<h2>How we build this</h2>
<p>Both tables come from one public model feed that lists every served model with the timestamp it first appeared and, where a switch-off has been announced, the date it ends. The filter keeps first-party models only: third-party routers, quantised mirrors and anonymous drops all carry timestamps but are not a lab shipping anything, and <code>:batch</code> or <code>:free</code> entries are the same weights behind a different endpoint, so they are dropped as duplicates of a row already here. Named tiers such as <code>-pro</code> are kept, because they are separate price points and choosing between them is the reason to be on this page.</p>
<p>Two dates matter and they are not the same date. <strong>{{ releases.updated }}</strong> is when this page's table was generated. The live feed behind it is at most six hours old and is checked when you load this page; a new model found in the live check is added to the top of the table and marked. Prices come from the router's rate card for that model, which is what you would be billed, and a model whose lab has not published a price shows a dash rather than a number.</p>
<p>What this page cannot tell you is what a lab said, or on what date they said it. For the announcement itself — the reasoning behind a price, the scope of a deprecation, the caveat on a benchmark — read the lab's own newsroom and social accounts. This is the operational layer underneath those posts: what is purchasable, what it costs, and what is about to stop working.</p>
</div>

<style>
/* Copied from the pricing tracker's page-local block: finops' shell has no
   global .wrap/.eye/.page-title, so these pages carry their own. */
.wrap{max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;padding:56px 24px}
.eye{font-family:"JetBrains Mono",ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#7AAFFF;margin:0 0 14px}
.page-title{font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,44px);line-height:1.08;margin:0 0 12px;color:#E6EAF2}
.lede{font-size:18px;color:#B6C0D2;max-width:62ch;margin:0 0 8px}
.back{display:inline-block;margin-top:40px;color:#7AAFFF;text-decoration:none}

h2{margin:44px 0 6px;font-size:22px;color:#E6EAF2}
h2 .count{font-size:13px;font-weight:400;color:#7A8598;margin-left:10px}
.note{color:#8b949e;font-size:14px;max-width:70ch;margin:0 0 18px}

.tracker-bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:16px;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;margin:32px 0 8px;padding:14px 16px;background:#161b22;border:1px solid #21262d;border-radius:12px}
.filters{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px}
.chip{font:inherit;font-size:13px;padding:6px 12px;border-radius:999px;border:1px solid #30363d;background:#0d1117;color:#B6C0D2;cursor:pointer}
.chip:hover{border-color:#7AAFFF;color:#E6EAF2}
.chip.is-on{background:#1f6feb;border-color:#1f6feb;color:#fff}
.chip:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #7AAFFF;outline-offset:2px}
.freshness{margin:0;font-size:13px;color:#8b949e}
.freshness strong{color:#B6C0D2;font-weight:600}
#liveCheck{display:block;font-size:12px}

.table-wrap{overflow-x:auto;border:1px solid #21262d;border-radius:12px;background:#161b22}
.tracker-table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px}
.tracker-table th{text-align:left;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7A8598;padding:12px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid #21262d;white-space:nowrap}
.tracker-table td{padding:11px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid #1b2028;color:#D5DCE8;vertical-align:top}
.tracker-table tbody tr:last-child td{border-bottom:0}
.tracker-table tbody tr:hover{background:#1b2028}
.tracker-table .num{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;white-space:nowrap}
.tracker-table td.left{text-align:left;white-space:nowrap}
.tracker-table code{font-size:12px}
.days{font-family:"JetBrains Mono",ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8b949e}
tr.is-urgent .days{color:#f85149;font-weight:600}
tr.is-urgent td:first-child{border-left:2px solid #f85149}
.is-live{background:#1f6feb}
.empty{color:#8b949e;font-size:14px;margin:14px 0}

.methodology{margin-top:60px;padding-top:40px;border-top:1px solid #21262d;color:#8b949e;font-size:14px}
.methodology h2{font-size:18px;margin-bottom:12px}
.methodology code{background:#0d1117;padding:1px 5px;border-radius:4px;color:#B6C0D2}
</style>

<script>
// Progressive enhancement only. The tables above are already in the HTML, so
// this never has to build them: it filters rows already on the page, keeps the
// retirement countdown honest between snapshot builds, and appends anything the
// live feed knows that the snapshot predates. A failed fetch changes nothing.
(function () {
  var fmt = function (v) {
    if (v === null || v === undefined) return '—';
    return '$' + v;
  };
  var ctx = function (n) {
    if (!n) return '—';
    return n >= 1e6 ? +(n / 1e6).toFixed(2) + 'M' : Math.round(n / 1000) + 'K';
  };

  function filterTo(lab) {
    document.querySelectorAll('.chip').forEach(function (c) {
      c.classList.toggle('is-on', c.dataset.lab === lab);
      c.setAttribute('aria-pressed', c.dataset.lab === lab ? 'true' : 'false');
    });
    [['shippedTable', 'shippedEmpty'], ['retiringTable', 'retiringEmpty']].forEach(function (pair) {
      var shown = 0;
      document.querySelectorAll('#' + pair[0] + ' tbody tr').forEach(function (row) {
        var on = lab === 'all' || row.dataset.lab === lab;
        row.hidden = !on;
        if (on) shown++;
      });
      document.getElementById(pair[1]).hidden = shown !== 0;
    });
  }

  document.querySelectorAll('.chip').forEach(function (chip) {
    chip.addEventListener('click', function () { filterTo(chip.dataset.lab); });
  });
  filterTo('all');

  // Recount the countdown: a snapshot is dated, a reader is not.
  var tick = function () {
    var today = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);
    document.querySelectorAll('#retiringTable tbody tr').forEach(function (row) {
      var cell = row.querySelector('[data-days]');
      if (!cell || !row.dataset.expires) return;
      var days = Math.round((Date.parse(row.dataset.expires + 'T00:00:00Z') - Date.parse(today + 'T00:00:00Z')) / 864e5);
      cell.textContent = days + 'd';
      row.classList.toggle('is-urgent', days <= 30);
    });
  };
  tick();

  fetch('/api/releases')
    .then(function (r) { return r.ok ? r.json() : null; })
    .then(function (d) {
      if (!d || !Array.isArray(d.releases)) return;
      var known = {};
      document.querySelectorAll('#shippedTable tbody tr').forEach(function (row) { known[row.dataset.id] = true; });
      var tbody = document.querySelector('#shippedTable tbody');
      var added = 0;

      d.releases.forEach(function (r) {
        if (known[r.id]) return;
        var tr = document.createElement('tr');
        tr.dataset.lab = r.provider;
        tr.dataset.id = r.id;
        tr.className = 'is-live';
        tr.innerHTML =
          '<td>' + r.date + '</td><td><strong>' + r.id + '</strong></td><td>' + r.provider +
          '</td><td class="num">' + fmt(r.in) + '</td><td class="num">' + fmt(r.out) +
          '</td><td class="num">' + ctx(r.ctx) + '</td>';
        tbody.insertBefore(tr, tbody.firstChild);
        added++;
      });

      document.getElementById('liveCheck').textContent =
        'Live feed checked ' + (d.updated || '') + (added ? ' · ' + added + ' new since the snapshot' : ' · up to date');
    })
    .catch(function () {});
})();
</script>

